	(text_box "The device core is supplied through the Vdd line while the I/O pads are supplied through the Vdd_IO line. Power supply decoupling capacitors (100 nF ceramic, 10 μF aluminum) should be placed as near as possible to pin 9 of the device (common design practice). It is possible to remove Vdd, maintaining Vdd_IO, without blocking the communication bus, in this condition the measurement chain is powered off.\n\nThe following recommendations apply to capacitor C1:\n-It must be connected as close as possible to pins 5 and 6 since very high current\npulses flow from C1 to pin 5 and 6. This avoid problems caused by inductive effects\ndue to the length of the copper strips.\n-It is highly recommended to use low ESR (max 200 mOhm)\nThe functionality of the device and the measured acceleration data are selectable and\naccessible through the I2C or SPI interfaces. When using the I2C, CS must be tied high (i.e.connected to Vdd_IO).\n\nThe functions, the threshold and the timing of the three interrupt pins (INT1_XL, INT2_XL,\nand INT_MAG/DRDY) can be completely programmed by the user through the I2 C/SPI\ninterface."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 189.23 16.51 0)
		(size 90.17 38.1)
		(margins 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524 0.9524)
		(stroke
			(width -0.0001)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
